      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">On the 5th of the week, 16 days in the month of Adar I, year 3 of the sabbatical cycle, an interculated year, which is year\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">4,693 A.M., in Damascus, Man\u1e63\u016br\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">b. Isaac b. Sa\u02bf\u012bd b. Pinhas gave the ring of security for Zuhra, the virgin, daughter of R. Jacob ha-Kohen, the scribe, according to</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">the cus[tom of the] small [sy]nagogue of the Babylonians. They fixed\u00a0 the mohar between them at seventy gold pieces: twenty-</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">five, the mohar of virgins, and the rest as an addition for mohar. And he advanced at the time of this security</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">fifteen good, fully weighed gold pieces. And at the time that he marries her, he shall pay her thirty-five,\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">the balance of the fifty. Rav Jacob, her father, accepted for her this ring of security, this [r]ing of security(!). He shall provide for</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">her [needs] until the time of her marriage to her husband. Valid is this writ of betrothal in the laws (courts) of Israel. May they build and prosper.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[Tw]enty delayed (gold pieces) are \"on his neck.\" May he be built by her. Bishr [b.] Isma\u02bf\u012bl\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">b. \u1e24\u0101tim testified to this and to all that is in this writ.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Isaac b. Samuel b. Nihm\u012b, witness.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Sa\u02bf\u012bd b. 'Uzayr \u1e6cavyomi whose soul is at rest testified to all th[at] is in this.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Elisha b. Moses ha-Kohen, witness.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Samuel b. Solomon b. \u02bfUzayr, witness.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Ezra b. Samuel b. Ezra, witness. And Moses b. Samuel b. \u1e24\u0101tim (who) r(ests in) E(den) testified.</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">Nissin b. Savoy, witness.\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">David b. Aaron, witness. Abraham the judge ha-Levi berabbi.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
